+# Daily Grind components
+
+Load `components/daily-grind.js` once with a module script. The components use
+native custom elements and open Shadow DOM; no dependencies or build are needed.
+
+## Coffee cards and hero
+
+`coffee-card` and `coffee-hero` accept three named slots:
+
+- `title`: an `h3` for a homepage card or an `h1` for the hero.
+- `description`: a paragraph.
+- `action`: a native anchor with its destination in `href`.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="title">Cold Brew</h3>
+  <p slot="description">Steeped for 18 hours for maximum smoothness.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/cold-brew"
+     aria-label="View details for Cold Brew">View Details</a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+Keep heading levels appropriate to the containing page and give repeated action
+labels a descriptive accessible name. Slot content remains in the document, so
+links and text are available before JavaScript loads. Layout and visual styling
+are applied when the components upgrade.
+
+## Navigation
+
+`daily-navigation` takes a brand in the `brand` slot and direct-child anchors in
+the default slot. The optional `logout-link` class gives an anchor an outlined
+appearance. Keep a skip link outside the sticky component.
+
+Below 761px, a native button toggles the links and reports its state through
+`aria-expanded`. Hidden links leave the tab order through `display: none`.
+Escape closes the menu and returns focus to the button. Following a link or
+crossing the breakpoint resets the menu. Listeners are removed when an instance
+disconnects and reattached when it reconnects.
+
+## Theme
+
+Components inherit the page font and the `--primary`, `--accent`, and
+`--focus-color` CSS properties, with defaults. Set `--hero-image` to a CSS
+`url(...)` to replace the hero photograph. Component styles, IDs, and navigation
+state are isolated per instance; the page owns the surrounding grid and spacing.
